1. Scope
   "The Software" refers to the CCPCOJ executable binaries (including csgoj-deploy), Web and Judge container images, and all proprietary components therein distributed by CSGrandeur ("the Licensor"). "The Documentation" refers to the manuals and images published in https://github.com/SZTU-ACM/CCPCOJ-2. By downloading, deploying, or using the Software or Documentation, you agree to be bound by this Agreement. No source code disclosure is promised, and all intellectual property rights remain exclusively with the Licensor.

2. Free Non-Commercial Grant for Education and Contests
   Subject to Section 3, the Licensor grants accredited universities, schools, non-profit research/educational institutions, and authorized programming contest committees (including ICPC, CCPC, provincial, invitational, and campus contests) a non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license to self-host and run the Software for teaching, training, and organizing such programming contests. Collecting customary team registration fees to cover contest operating expenses or displaying event sponsors on contest pages/scoreboards does not violate this non-commercial condition.

3. Prohibited Commercial Uses and Restrictions
   Without a separate prior written commercial license from the Licensor (csgrandeur@gmail.com), you may NOT:
   (a) use the Software for commercial training agencies, paid courses, paid training camps, or paid online judge accounts;
   (b) sell, rent, redistribute, or offer paid SaaS hosting, paid contest-platform rental, or paid deployment/maintenance services based on the Software;
   (c) bundle or embed the Software into commercial software, hardware appliances, or commercial offerings;
   (d) reverse-engineer, decompile, disassemble, decrypt, or extract proprietary program components from the binaries or container images, except to the extent such restriction is expressly prohibited by applicable law;
   (e) remove, obscure, or alter any copyright, attribution, or brand notices in the Software or Documentation.

4. Third-Party Open-Source Carve-Out
   Operating system packages and third-party open-source libraries included within the container images remain governed by their respective open-source licenses. Nothing in Section 3 restricts your rights under those third-party licenses with respect to such third-party components.

5. Commercial Licensing and Future Relicensing
   Commercial use requires a separate paid written agreement via csgrandeur@gmail.com. The Licensor reserves the right to modify these terms or relicense future versions (including under standard open-source licenses); any such change applies prospectively only and does not retroactively alter the license of previously released versions or images. Contributors to the public repository grant the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, sublicensable right to use and distribute their contributions across free, commercial, and future open-source editions.

6. Disclaimer of Warranty and Limitation of Liability
   THE SOFTWARE AND DOCUMENTATION ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, CONTEST INTERRUPTION, DATA LOSS, OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR DOCUMENTATION.
